From a63cc9a8c81d6282fb3d38930d18c6b06a9a264d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devon Openheim <devopenm@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 12:29:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: vendor-prefixes: add ASR Microelectronics

Document the `asr` vendor prefix (ASR Microelectronics), required by
the ASR1802S SoC and P298 board support.

Only the SoC vendor prefix is registered. The board is a Notion design sold by
operator Ooredoo under carrier branding, but the compatible string uses the SoC
vendor (`asr`) plus the hardware platform code (P298, from the board silkscreen,
the U-Boot banner "ASR KAGU EVB P298" and ASR's own kernel build string), so a
`notion` prefix would be registered without ever being used. The operator SKU
string is also deliberately unused: an unrelated MediaTek MT7621A product is
sold as "R291" too, which would make it ambiguous across two devices.

Signed-off-by: Devon Openheim <devopenm@proton.me>

---

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/vendor-prefixes.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/vendor-prefixes.yaml
@@ -178,6 +178,8 @@
     description: ASIX Electronics Corporation
   "^aspeed,.*":
     description: ASPEED Technology Inc.
+  "^asr,.*":
+    description: ASR Microelectronics Co., Ltd.
   "^asrock,.*":
     description: ASRock Inc.
   "^asteralabs,.*":
